<title>THAILAND: Thai Petrochemical signs $500 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Thai Petrochemical signs $500 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Petrochemical Industry Plc said on Thursday it signed a loan agreement worth $500 million with the International Finance Corp, the private arm of the World Bank.  </p>
<p>The funds will be used to finance the construction of its fully integrated petrochemical complex in eastern Rayong province, Thai Petrochemical said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand.</p>
<p>The loan will have term of 9 to 11 years with annual interest rate of LIBOR plus 1.775 percentage points, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
